        <section id="api-json" class="api-card">
          <h2>Catalog API endpoints</h2>
          <p>
            Use these catalog endpoints for search, records, and facets.
            The <code>format</code> query parameter is the most reliable option when IDs include dots
            (for example <code>oocihm.N_00591</code>).
          </p>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Catalog API endpoints</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Endpoint</th>
                  <th scope="col">Method and path</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Search endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET /catalog?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Single record endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET /catalog/:id?format=json</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Facet endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET /catalog/facet/:facet_id?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Single record export endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET /catalog/:id?format=marc|marcxml|xml</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 id="api-params">Catalog query parameters</h3>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table api-table--params">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Catalog query parameters</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                  <th scope="col">Type</th>
                  <th scope="col">Description</th>
                  <th scope="col">Values / Default</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>q</code></th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <td>Search query text.</td>
                  <td>Default: empty string</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>search_field</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Search field to run the query against.</td>
                  <td><code>all_fields</code>, <code>full_title_tsim</code>, <code>author_tsim</code>, <code>subject_tsim</code>, <code>tx_gen</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>lang</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Response locale.</td>
                  <td><code>en</code>, <code>fr</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>page</code></th>
                  <td>integer</td>
                  <td>Result page number (starts at 1).</td>
                  <td>Default: <code>1</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>per_page</code></th>
                  <td>integer</td>
                  <td>Number of results per page.</td>
                  <td><code>10</code>, <code>20</code>, <code>50</code>, <code>100</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>sort</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Sort key for result ordering.</td>
                  <td><code>relevance</code>, <code>year-desc</code>, <code>year-asc</code>, <code>date-added-desc</code>, <code>date-added-asc</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>f[field_name][]=value</code></th>
                  <td>array</td>
                  <td>Facet filters to constrain results.</td>
                  <td><code>pub_date_ssim</code>, <code>language_ssim_str</code>, <code>depositor_tsim_str</code>, <code>subject_ssim_str</code>, <code>author_ssm_str</code>, <code>collectionen_path</code>, <code>collectionfr_path</code>, <code>serial_title_str</code>, <code>is_issue_str</code>, <code>is_serial_str</code>. Example: <code>f[language_ssim_str][]=English</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>range[pub_date_ssim][begin]</code><br><code>range[pub_date_ssim][end]</code></th>
                  <td>integer</td>
                  <td>Publication-year range filter.</td>
                  <td>Example: <code>1900</code> to <code>1910</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>format</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Output format for the response.</td>
                  <td>Search: <code>html</code>, <code>json</code>; Single record: <code>html</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>marc</code>, <code>marcxml</code>, <code>xml</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <h3 id="api-structure">Catalog response structure</h3>
          <p>
            A search request such as
            <code>/catalog?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code>
            returns:
          </p>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Catalog response structure fields</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Field</th>
                  <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>links</code></th>
                  <td>Navigation URLs (<code>self</code>, <code>next</code>, <code>last</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>meta.pages</code></th>
                  <td>Page state and counts (<code>current_page</code>, <code>total_pages</code>, <code>limit_value</code>, <code>total_count</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>data[]</code></th>
                  <td>Search result records with <code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>attributes</code>, and <code>links.self</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>included[]</code></th>
                  <td>Reusable API objects for facet definitions, search fields, and sort options.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Catalog response structure in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">JSON</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>{
    "links": {"self": "...", "next": "...", "last": "..."},
    "meta": {
        "pages": {
            "current_page": 1,
            "total_pages": 246,
            "limit_value": 10,
            "total_count": 2454
        }
    },
    "data": [
        {
            "id": "oocihm.N_00591",
            "type": "Newspaper",
            "attributes": {
                "title": "Keneder adler",
                "published_ssm": {
                    "type": "document_value",
                    "attributes": {"label": "Published", "value": "..."}
                },
                "language_ssim": {
                    "type": "document_value",
                    "attributes": {"label": "Language", "value": "..."}
                }
            },
            "links": {"self": "http://localhost:3000/catalog/oocihm.N_00591?lang=en"}
        }
    ],
    "included": [
        {"type": "facet", "id": "language_ssim_str"},
        {"type": "search_field", "id": "all_fields"},
        {"type": "sort", "id": "date-added-desc"}
    ]
}</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <p>
            Many <code>attributes.*.attributes.value</code> values are HTML fragments for display.
            If you are building a pure data pipeline, plan to strip or sanitize markup.
          </p>
          <h3 id="api-examples">Catalog examples</h3>
          <h4>Example 1: Default catalog JSON response</h4>
          <p>Fetch the default catalog payload and read total result count.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Catalog default JSON example">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

BASE_URL = "http://localhost:3000"

response = requests.get(
    f"{BASE_URL}/catalog",
    params={"search_field": "all_fields", "q": "", "format": "json"},
    timeout=30,
)
response.raise_for_status()
catalog = response.json()
print(catalog["meta"]["pages"]["total_count"])</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h4>Example 2: Query with sorting and pagination</h4>
          <p>Run a keyword query and control order, page size, and page number.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Catalog sorting and pagination example">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

BASE_URL = "http://localhost:3000"

response = requests.get(
    f"{BASE_URL}/catalog",
    params={
        "q": "maps",
        "search_field": "all_fields",
        "sort": "date-added-desc",
        "per_page": 20,
        "page": 1,
        "format": "json",
    },
    timeout=30,
)
response.raise_for_status()
maps = response.json()</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h4>Example 3: Facet filters</h4>
          <p>Apply facet constraints to narrow results by language and collection path.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Catalog facet filter examples">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

BASE_URL = "http://localhost:3000"

english_response = requests.get(
    f"{BASE_URL}/catalog",
    params={
        "q": "",
        "search_field": "all_fields",
