        <section id="api-iiif-query" class="api-card">
          <h2>IIIF API</h2>
          <h3 id="iiif-endpoints">IIIF API endpoints</h3>
          <p>
            IIIF is a shared framework for publishing, linking, and reusing digital cultural heritage objects.
            IIIF resources are published as Linked Open Data using
            <a href="https://json-ld.org/">JSON-LD</a>, which is a JSON serialization of
            <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-concepts/">RDF</a>.
            This lets clients follow stable identifiers across manifests, canvases, annotations, and image services.
          </p>
          <p>Endpoints are grouped in the Image, Manifest, and Content Search sections below.</p>
          <p>
            Official IIIF API docs:
            <a href="https://iiif.io/api/">iiif.io/api</a>.
          </p>
          <h3 id="iiif-image">IIIF Image API</h3>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">IIIF Image API endpoints</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Endpoint</th>
                  <th scope="col">Path</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Image info endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET {image_service}/info.json</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Image render endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET {image_service}/{region}/{size}/{rotation}/{quality}.{format}</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            Full specification:
            <a href="https://iiif.io/api/image/2.1/">IIIF Image API 2.1</a>.
          </p>
          <h4>Response formats</h4>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">IIIF Image API response formats</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Endpoint</th>
                  <th scope="col">Response format</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Image info endpoint (<code>info.json</code>)</th>
                  <td>JSON (IIIF Image API)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Image render endpoint</th>
                  <td>Binary image bytes (for example <code>image/jpeg</code>)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table api-table--params">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">IIIF Image API request parameters</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                  <th scope="col">Type</th>
                  <th scope="col">Description</th>
                  <th scope="col">Values / Examples</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>region</code></th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <td>Image region to extract.</td>
                  <td><code>full</code>, <code>x,y,w,h</code>, <code>pct:x,y,w,h</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>size</code></th>
                  <td>string</td>
                  <td>Target output dimensions.</td>
                  <td><code>full</code>, <code>w,</code>, <code>,h</code>, <code>w,h</code>, <code>pct:n</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>rotation</code></th>
                  <td>number</td>
                  <td>Output rotation angle.</td>
                  <td><code>0</code>, <code>90</code>, <code>180</code>, <code>270</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>quality</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Rendering quality profile supported by the service.</td>
                  <td><code>default</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>gray</code>, <code>bitonal</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>format</code></th>
                  <td>enum</td>
                  <td>Binary image format returned by the endpoint.</td>
                  <td><code>jpg</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <h3>IIIF Image API response shape</h3>
          <p><code>info.json</code> returns JSON metadata:</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF info.json response in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">JSON</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>{
    "@context": "http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json",
    "@id": "{image_service}",
    "protocol": "http://iiif.io/api/image",
    "width": 3936,
    "height": 3200,
    "sizes": [{"width": 123, "height": 100}, "..."],
    "tiles": [{"width": 512, "height": 512, "scaleFactors": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]}],
    "profile": [
        "http://iiif.io/api/image/2/level1.json",
        {
            "formats": ["jpg"],
            "qualities": ["bitonal", "default", "gray", "color"],
            "supports": ["regionByPx", "sizeByW", "rotationBy90s", "..."]
        }
	    ]
}</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h3 id="iiif-image-examples">IIIF Image API examples</h3>
          <h4>Example: IIIF image requests</h4>
          <p>Use the image service to inspect capabilities and request common derivatives.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF Image API requests in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

def iiif_image_url(
    service_id,
    region="full",
    size="full",
    rotation="0",
    quality="default",
    fmt="jpg",
):
    return f"{service_id}/{region}/{size}/{rotation}/{quality}.{fmt}"

service_id = "https://image-tor.canadiana.ca/iiif/2/69429%2Fc2025000026xr85"

# Discover capabilities
info = requests.get(f"{service_id}/info.json", timeout=30).json()
print(info["width"], info["height"])  # 3936 3200

# Full image resized to width 500
img_small = requests.get(iiif_image_url(service_id, size="500,"), timeout=30)
print(img_small.headers["Content-Type"])  # image/jpeg

# Crop by percent region, then resize
img_crop = requests.get(
    iiif_image_url(service_id, region="pct:25,25,50,50", size="800,"),
    timeout=30,
)

# Rotated output
img_rotated = requests.get(iiif_image_url(service_id, size="500,", rotation="90"), timeout=30)

# Alternate quality
img_gray = requests.get(iiif_image_url(service_id, size="500,", quality="gray"), timeout=30)</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h4>Example: Binary image response</h4>
          <p>Read a rendered image response and verify MIME type before using raw bytes.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Binary image response in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

response = requests.get(
    "https://image-tor.canadiana.ca/iiif/2/69429%2Fc2025000026xr85/full/500,/0/default.jpg",
    timeout=30,
)
response.raise_for_status()

print(response.headers["Content-Type"])  # image/jpeg
binary_jpeg = response.content            # bytes
print(len(binary_jpeg))</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h3 id="iiif-manifest">IIIF Presentation API (Manifest)</h3>
          <p>
            The example below is based on manifest <code>m2025000007606h</code>
            (collection <code>69429</code>). It is a IIIF Presentation 3 manifest with
            <code>842</code> canvases.
          </p>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">IIIF Manifest endpoint</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Endpoint</th>
                  <th scope="col">Path</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Manifest endpoint</th>
                  <td><code>GET {presentation_service}/69429/m2025000007606h</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            Full specification:
            <a href="https://iiif.io/api/presentation/3.0/">IIIF Presentation API 3.0</a>.
          </p>
          <h4>Response formats</h4>
          <div class="api-table-wrap">
            <table class="api-table">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">IIIF Manifest response formats</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Endpoint</th>
                  <th scope="col">Response format</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Manifest endpoint</th>
                  <td>JSON (IIIF Presentation 3)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <h4>Manifest response shape (Presentation 3)</h4>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Manifest response shape in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
